  "live_records": {
    "q-77080": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77080",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Let $a=47$ and $n=7.$ Find integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a=qn+r,$ where $0\\le r<n.$ Then, $r=$",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing $47$ by $7$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n6<47÷7<7.\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So $q=6.$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by computing $r=a-qn.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=47-(6)(7)=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write $47=qn+r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}47={{6}_{⏟}}_{q}\\cdot 7+{{5}_{⏟}}_{r}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $r=5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
