    "q-77088": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77088",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Let $a=-50$ and $n=7.$ Find integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a=qn+r,$ where $0\\le r<n,$ and determine $q\\cdot r.$",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing $-50$ by $7$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n-8<-50÷7<-7.\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So $q=-8.$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by solving $r=a-qn.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=-50-(-8)(7)=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write $-50=qn+r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-50={{(-8)}_{⏟}}_{q}\\cdot 7+{{6}_{⏟}}_{r}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $q\\cdot r=-8\\cdot 6=-48.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
